        name = "Tabard of the Hand",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete the Draenei-only reward chain and its scripted demolition escort.\n\n1. Use a regular Draenei character; Lightforged Draenei do not qualify for the final tabard quest. Any class works, including Death Knight. Go to Blood Watch in Bloodmyst Isle and enable Trivial Quests. The old guide's level-100 Class Trial, garrison and Legion-introduction travel steps are unnecessary.\n\n2. Speak to Vindicator Aesom at Blood Watch (55.6, 55.4) and take What We Know... (9753). Deliver it to Exarch Admetius inside the nearby building (52.6, 53.2). You do not need to complete every quest on Azuremyst or Bloodmyst first.\n\n3. Accept What We Don't Know... (9756). Let Admetius disguise you, question the blood elf prisoner in the cage just downhill, then return to Admetius. Stay in Blood Watch while disguised so the spell does not fail. Accept Vindicator's Rest (9760).\n\n4. Go west to Vindicator Corin at Vindicator's Rest (30.6, 46.6). Take Clearing the Way (9761), kill the requested Sunhawk Agents and Sunhawk Saboteurs around the Vector Coil, southwest around 17.0, 55.0, and return to Corin.\n\n5. Speak to Demolitionist Legoso beside Corin (30.8, 46.6) and accept Ending Their World (9759). If Legoso is absent, another player may be escorting him; let that event finish and check again. Complete Clearing the Way before assuming he is missing permanently.\n\n6. Follow and protect Legoso all the way up the Vector Coil to around 14.8, 54.9. Let him place and detonate his explosives, then defeat Sironas when the event makes her attackable. Stay with the escort until the quest objective actually completes; killing nearby blood elves alone is insufficient.\n\n7. Return to Exarch Admetius at Blood Watch (52.6, 53.2) and turn in Ending Their World. Walk outside to the welcoming crowd. Speak to Prophet Velen there around 54.0, 55.5 and accept and complete The Unwritten Prophecy (9762) for the tabard. Do not leave immediately for the permanent Velen in the Exodar and miss the ceremony.\n\n8. Equip the tabard and check your appearance collection. Once learned, the appearance can be used by other eligible Alliance characters. If Aesom has no starting quest, check your log for a later chain step; the comments also report relogging or accepting and abandoning a local Blood Watch quest making the starter appear.",
