        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Complete the short eligible Paladin class quest, breaking its weapons at the Black Anvil.\n\n1. For the direct reward, use a Blood Elf Paladin of level 20 or higher. This is the original Blood Knight Tabard, not the later Blood Knight Champion's Tabard. The old epic-Charger chain and its expensive materials are no longer the acquisition route.\n\n2. Go to Avaros Dawnglaive in the Orgrimmar barracks, Valley of Honor (73.3, 47.0). Enable Trivial Quests, take Meet With Avaros Dawnglaive if offered, then accept Weapons of Darkness (28473). The relevant quests moved here; do not search the old Silvermoon headquarters.\n\n3. Enter the original Blackrock Depths dungeon beneath Blackrock Mountain. Approach from Searing Gorge around 35.0, 85.0, descend the interior chains to the central tomb, then follow the lower passage toward the quarry and dungeon portal. Use the original five-player dungeon, not an anniversary raid queue.\n\n4. Kill and loot Anvilrage/Dark Iron dwarves near the dungeon entrance until you have 5 Elemental-Imbued Weapons in your bags. Looting them does not complete the objective: all five must also be broken. Dwarves in the entrance quarry can supply the weapons too.\n\n5. Reach the Black Anvil beside Lord Incendius on the Detention Block floor (56.4, 31.1). For a direct route, take the gate immediately left of the entrance into the Dark Iron Highway, then follow the highway RIGHT toward Shadowforge City and the anvil bridge. Bael'gar is the opposite direction. Clear Incendius and nearby enemies, then use each of the five quest weapons while standing at the anvil.\n\n6. Return to Avaros in Orgrimmar and turn in Weapons of Darkness. Choose the helm reward and collect the additional Blood Knight Tabard. Equip the tabard to confirm the learned appearance.\n\n7. If you completed the eligible Horde paladin version previously, check Garyl's tabard inventory in Orgrimmar (47.5, 75.5). Tauren-paladin comments document buying the tabard after their Weapons of Darkness completion. The reliable new-character route above uses a Blood Elf Paladin; Alliance vendor purchases and non-paladin loopholes do not establish a usable appearance on those characters.",
