        itemId = 31776,
        name = "Consortium Tabard",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Repeat Consortium insignia or warbead turn-ins, or Heroic Mana-Tombs, until Exalted.\n\n1. Check The Consortium reputation. Either faction can earn it. At Exalted, skip to step 6. This faction is separate from Kurenai and The Mag'har, even though all three can accept Obsidian Warbeads.\n\n2. For the dungeon route, enter Mana-Tombs, the north wing of Auchindoun in Terokkar Forest (39.6, 57.7). Set Dungeon Difficulty to HEROIC. Normal Mana-Tombs helps early standings but has a reputation cap and is not the finishing route.\n\n3. Clear the Heroic trash while leaving EVERY boss alive. Bypass Pandemonius, Tavarok and Nexus-Prince Shaffar, loot the enemies, return outside, reset and repeat. Avoiding boss kills allows the trash route to be reset without creating a Heroic boss save. Smaller pulls are sensible if a large dragged pack fails to award reputation, as a later reply reports.\n\n4. If you prefer outdoor turn-ins, reach Friendly with the Consortium at Aeris Landing in western Nagrand, then give batches of 10 Obsidian Warbeads to Gezhe (31.4, 57.6) for the repeatable More Obsidian Warbeads quest. This advances the Consortium, not your faction's talbuk reputation.\n\n5. Farm those beads from Nagrand ogres at Laughing Skull Ruins (46.0, 23.0) or Warmaul Hill (29.0, 26.0), or buy them. Repeat Heroic trash clears and/or eligible bead turn-ins until Consortium Exalted. If you kill a Heroic boss accidentally, use the bead route or return after the lockout resets.\n\n6. Buy Consortium Tabard from Karaaz at the Stormspire in Netherstorm (43.5, 34.5), or from Paulsta'ats at Aeris Landing in Nagrand (30.5, 57.0). Both sell the same tabard for up to 1 gold before discounts. Only one purchase is needed; equip it to learn the appearance.",
