        itemId = 31404,
        name = "Green Trophy Tabard of the Illidari",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Finish the short Crimson Watch quest chain; current completion grants access to both tabard colors.\n\n1. Use a character of level 25 or higher and go to Shadowmoon Valley in OUTLAND, not Draenor. Either faction and any class can earn both Illidari tabards. You do not need to be a Demon Hunter, finish the Demon Hunter campaign or enter Black Temple.\n\n2. Find Val'zareq the Conqueror and his patrol on the Path of Conquest, roughly between 50.5, 59.0 and 53.0, 68.5. Kill him, loot The Journal of Val'zareq (31345), then use the journal from your bags to start The Journal of Val'zareq: Portends of War (10793). Search along the patrol route rather than waiting at a single spawn pin.\n\n3. Take the journal quest to the Crystal Prison at 51.4, 72.8. Speak to the trapped Marcus Auralion in the crystal and turn it in. Accept Battle of the Crimson Watch (10781) when you are ready: it starts a wave event at this location.\n\n4. Remain by the prison, defeat every wave and then Torloth the Magnificent. Wait through the scripted pauses until the final enemy is attackable, and stay until the quest marks complete. On a high-level Retail character the original group recommendation is usually unnecessary; bring help if you are doing it at the content's level.\n\n5. Return to A'dal in Shattrath's Terrace of Light (54.0, 44.6) and turn in Battle of the Crimson Watch. Current Retail awards BOTH Green Trophy Tabard of the Illidari and Purple Trophy Tabard of the Illidari. Choose any accompanying ring reward and collect the tabards; no random-color reroll is needed.\n\n6. Equip both tabards and check both appearances. If an older character already completed the quest but lacks one color, speak to Linsa nearby (58.6, 46.6) and check the lost-tabard dialogue for that completed quest. The old auto-loot, wait-two-hours and item-restoration tricks are not part of a fresh Retail completion.",
        sourceType = "Quests",
        effect = "Cosmetic tabard appearance. Wearing this tabard does not grant faction reputation in dungeons.",
